{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi","id":1128752,"title":"Nephandi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-14T04:19:59-07:00","id":1128752,"title":"Nephandi","content":"Hello everyone, I hope you're having a great day.<br /> Ok, so I've been working on a character which I've been roleplaying so far for like 4 years now.<br /> The character has been struggling for so long since she was 6-7 years old until she reached 23. I'll leave the details for later. Her life has been shit, full of bad treatment and treason. She got sick of it and I'm thinking of making her go Nephandi except idk how she's gonna cross the caul so I might need some ideas, thanks in advance &lt;3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T06:31:39-07:00","id":1128781,"title":"","content":"Ideas about what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T07:15:44-07:00","id":1128795,"title":"","content":"There's an important thing, Leonardo: An evil, murdering, abusive, a*holish Mage is not necessarily a Nephandus. Not even most Infernalists are necessarily Nephandi.<br /> <br /> They are just evil Mages. A Nephandus is like an evil Mage, squared times ten. They are the worst of the worst.<br /> So, there needs to be a reason for the character to actually fall for the Nephandi, after a lifetime of bad treatment and treason - I mean, she'd probably be extra suspicious of them, not less. Also, people can only voluntarily walk the cauls - no trickery, no force.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is basically this: Don't fall for the way too common trope of '<i>Angry Mage becomes evil, thus Nephandus!'</i>. It's way overused. Clich\u00e9, really.<br /> Simply becoming an evil, Magick slinging nasty Piece O' Work without any Nephandus influence can be way more creative, and is probably way more common.<br /> <br /> Simply consider the nastiest people you know out there, and imagine one of them suddenly having Magick in RL. Yeah. No Caul walking needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":".  Typo fixings. 08-14-2017, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T07:46:30-07:00","id":1128812,"title":"","content":"Indeed. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Voormas\" target=\"_blank\">Voormas</a>, one of the evilest mages out there and the most iconic villan of Mage isn't a Nephandi. <br /> <br /> If you had enough with your mage faction, you can always go rogue. Fuck the Traditions/Technocracy! , I'm not standing their bullshit anymore!. Rogue mages have left their faction and function outside the system. Usually, they're supposed to be regarded as betrayers and punished, but the reality of mage's life it's that the Traditions usually haven't resources to pursue every deserter, and concentrate only in the worst ones. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T14:11:42-07:00","id":1128958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1128795#post1128795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an important thing, Leonardo: An evil, murdering, abusive, a*holish Mage is not necessarily a Nephandus. Not even most Infernalists are necessarily Nephandi.<br /> <br /> They are just evil Mages. A Nephandus is like an evil Mage, squared times ten. They are the worst of the worst.<br /> So, there needs to be a reason for the character to actually fall for the Nephandi, after a lifetime of bad treatment and treason - I mean, she'd probably be extra suspicious of them, not less. Also, people can only voluntarily walk the cauls - no trickery, no force.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is basically this: Don't fall for the way too common trope of '<i>Angry Mage becomes evil, thus Nephandus!'</i>. It's way overused. Clich\u00e9, really.<br /> Simply becoming an evil, Magick slinging nasty Piece O' Work without any Nephandus influence can be way more creative, and is probably way more common.<br /> <br /> Simply consider the nastiest people you know out there, and imagine one of them suddenly having Magick in RL. Yeah. No Caul walking needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second that.<br /> <br /> IMHO a non nephandic is even more a bad guy, because he could be doing good things, could be good.<br /> A Nephandus is somewhat impaired in this regard due to the inverted Avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T07:12:18-07:00","id":1129770,"title":"","content":"As others have said, going Nephandi is quite an extreme choice and perhaps an unnecessary one.<br /> <br /> If you still were interested, I think there are a few ways. But the easiest would be making contact with a Nephandi, Black Spiral Dancer, Bane, etc that would help them get to a Caul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T01:05:53-07:00","id":1130742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi#post1128752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (...)<br /> Ok, so I've been working on a character which I've been roleplaying so far for like 4 years now. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>How does she see the Nephandi - how does she perceive them as True Mages; compared to herself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T16:05:12-07:00","id":1133205,"title":"","content":"I agree that Nephandus is an extreme step. Nephandi have the additional problem of attracting universal opposition. A Mage who decides they want revenge, but goes &quot;evil&quot; while remaining officially within their Tradition, is far more dangerous. From a political standpoint, Mages that stand to benefit from her actions might look the other way, or even side with her in some circumstances.<br /> <br /> Also, a PC &quot;evil&quot; Mage has the option of changing their mind, and thus can evolve into narratives other than vengeance/evil. A Nephandus, on the other hand, is basically stuck in &quot;F* the world&quot; mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T04:22:50-07:00","id":1133319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1133205#post1133205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (...) A Nephandus, on the other hand, is basically stuck in &quot;F* the world&quot; mode.</div> </div> </div> </div>In how many places across Mage: the Ascension is this written?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T04:54:47-07:00","id":1133322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1133319#post1133319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In how many places across Mage: the Ascension is this written?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...you invert your avatar, right? That's like the definition of &quot;THIS CHARACTER IS PERMANENTLY EVIL NOW.&quot; It's kind of the core feature of being Nephandi. They're the Bad Mages. That's the function they serve from a game design perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T05:02:39-07:00","id":1133323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1133322#post1133322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean...you invert your avatar, right? That's like the definition of &quot;THIS CHARACTER IS PERMANENTLY EVIL NOW.&quot; It's kind of the core feature of being Nephandi. They're the Bad Mages. That's the function they serve from a game design perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware that it is described more or less like you wrote in one or two books of M:tA ; I was wondering in how many places across Mage: the Ascension this (and similar ones) line of thought is written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-24-2017, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T08:13:58-07:00","id":1133379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was wondering in how many places across Mage: the Ascension this (and similar ones) line of thought is written.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>All of it. </b>Literally, every time the topic it's mentioned.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to count, but just read every Basic, including M20, read the Book of Madness (both editions), read the Storyteller's handbook. Wherever Nephandi are mentioned evil it's assumed.<br /> <br /> A better question would be <i>in how many places across Mage: the Ascension is this line of tought contradicted.</i> I know one <i>potential </i>instance: Archmaster/Oracle level intervention MAY be able to stray a Nephandi from it's evil path. That's it. If super-mages with ST fiat powers aren't involved, a fully initiated Nephandi it's permanently evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:04:18-07:00","id":1133402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1133379#post1133379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>All of it. </b>Literally, every time the topic it's mentioned.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to count, but just read every Basic, including M20, read the Book of Madness (both editions), read the Storyteller's handbook. Wherever Nephandi are mentioned evil it's assumed.<br /> <br /> A better question would be <i>in how many places across Mage: the Ascension is this line of tought contradicted.</i> I know one <i>potential </i>instance: Archmaster/Oracle level intervention MAY be able to stray a Nephandi from it's evil path. That's it. If super-mages with ST fiat powers aren't involved, a fully initiated Nephandi it's permanently evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't you say that this makes the Nephandi less engaging?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T10:08:23-07:00","id":1133431,"title":"","content":"It depends. I think Nephandy are flawed, but not because they're hard to set straight.<br /> <br /> I think that overplaying their edginess and their attitude of &quot;evil for the sake of evil&quot; it's bad, it makes them cartoonish and predictable. One can't understand how they can be so good at infiltration when everything they do it's edgelord level evil. But the same can be said of clown Marauders. It's not the evil insanity what's bad, but the way it's portrayed (both by rookie ST and the books).<br /> <br /> I think that the Fallen and the Fall have their uses. They're good boogeyman. They represent a force that's so trascendental that it's horrifying in its own right. Becoming one it's like dying in a realistic setting, would Death be engaging if everyone can resurrect?. It should be something that can happen to the characters, much like being erased from Reality trough Paradox/Hubris can happen. Sadly, there isn't a lot of reason of why one would want to become a Nephandus.<br /> <br /> I think it's ok for the Fallen to be very hard to rescue, milacurous even, because that reinforces the idea of The Fall as something really dire. You cannot just repent, and be done with it. Actions have consequences, some sins can't be wished away...But I don't think it should be *impossible*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T10:20:54-07:00","id":1133434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1133431#post1133431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sadly, there isn't a lot of reason of why one would want to become a Nephandus.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is this short story on pages 81-83 of the <i>Book of Shadows - Player's Guide</i> which I see as describing the Nephandi as powerful, enlightened and possessing a close-knit sense of unity and familiarity between each other. I think these are good reasons to join the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do think going back from being a Nephandus should be a step perhaps even more life-changing than becoming a Nephandus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-24-2017, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T12:52:23-07:00","id":1135557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1133431#post1133431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends. I think Nephandy are flawed, but not because they're hard to set straight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Nephandi as a narrative tool are somewhat counter-intuitive. They are basically a sledgehammer, but you need to use them like a scalpel. Since the WoD is all about shades of gray, it's easy to blot out the entire picture if you use too much black.<br /> <br /> Which is why I think reaching for them as the manifestation of PC trauma isn't generally advisable. Within canon, Nephandi DON'T turn back. It's a one-way ticket to damnation. Quiet is a better tool for handling traumatized PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T11:55:34-07:00","id":1138361,"title":"","content":"The signature character Amanda from 2nd edition appears to have turned back, but it took death, reincarnation, and the intervention of a half-millennium old archmaster of Entropy to get her there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T12:13:02-07:00","id":1138364,"title":"","content":"There's a line somewhere that you have a limited number of years to kill a Barrabus before the inversion becomes permanent. It is entirely possible that Senex's relevant skill was being really good at killing people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T13:48:15-07:00","id":1138386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1138364#post1138364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It is entirely possible that Senex's relevant skill was being really good at killing people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just the skill I'd expect from the Traditions' man who tries to present himself as the supposed &quot;redeemer of a Widderslainte&quot; !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-07-2017, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T14:37:40-07:00","id":1138401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1138364#post1138364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a line somewhere that you have a limited number of years to kill a Barrabus before the inversion becomes permanent. It is entirely possible that Senex's relevant skill was being really good at killing people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coincidentally, I read that line today. It's in the Revised Storytellers Handbook, the large chapter about Avatars. Widderslainte Avatars are always inverted (Which makes sense, because they get born with one), but a Barrabus' Avatar is not instantly inverted after the cauls - the Avatar has X years time before inversion is final, equal to the avatar rating.<br /> <br /> ..and the book even mentions that if the Avatar notices the starting inversion, that it might try to kill or get the Nephandus killed before that happens. Heh.<br /> Once the Barrabus' Avatar is inverted, killing them will just get you a new Widderslainte at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T05:50:07-07:00","id":1141032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1133322#post1133322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean...you invert your avatar, right? That's like the definition of &quot;THIS CHARACTER IS PERMANENTLY EVIL NOW.&quot; It's kind of the core feature of being Nephandi. They're the Bad Mages. That's the function they serve from a game design perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is so absurd to me.<br /> Maybe Mage: The Ascension is Mage: The Awakening through the point of view of Seers of the Throne and their internal civil war, technocrats vs traditions, while the heirs of Atlantis- the nephandi- are persecuted and hunted through countless incarnations, without choice or say in the matter. The seers simply say nephandi are tainted, corrupted, bearers of inverted avatars and deserving of death without judgement.<br /> This is why the &quot;evil&quot; or bad label seems so non-sense, it's just military propaganda, since when did universal morality and ethics mattered to reality bending humans? Who watch the watchers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T06:50:28-07:00","id":1141050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1141032#post1141032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is so absurd to me.<br /> Maybe Mage: The Ascension is Mage: The Awakening through the point of view of Seers of the Throne and their internal civil war, technocrats vs traditions, while the heirs of Atlantis- the nephandi- are persecuted and hunted through countless incarnations, without choice or say in the matter. The seers simply say nephandi are tainted, corrupted, bearers of inverted avatars and deserving of death without judgement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. It also explains why the descriptions of the Nephandi are so contradictory and full of mistakes:<br /> <br /> The Caul is said many times to be the way one becomes the Nephandi, yet for two out of the three original Nephandi factions a totally different initiation is described. The Infernal Nephandi get initiated through interaction with an Infernal Lady or an Infernal Lord ; while the Malfean Nephandi go through the Black Spiral.<br /> In the <i>Thousand Hells</i> Kuei-Jin book, True Mages who make a Soul Pact with a Yama Queen or King are described as being \u201cNephandi with exotic patrons\u201d - this is another contradiction of the writings that say that you need to go through a Caul to join the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> The only Widderslainte described in M:tA, in the <i>Fallen Tower - Las Vegas Citybook</i>, has her True Mage Essence listed as Primordial; which is not a Widderslainte True Mage Essence. She is also, despite being a Widderslainte, described as going into a 'Caul'.<br /> <br /> Despite there being outlined a very clear divide into the three different factions of the Nephandi - with each having vastly different beings as Patrons - this separation and the factions are completely ignored every time when the Nephandi are actually described - instead, the writing refers to ambiguous 'Dark Lords' or 'Dark Patrons' of the Nephandi. Seemingly important Nephandi like The Jade Demon or Galarius are effectively faction-less if you go by their descriptions.<br /> <br /> Galarius, a Nephandus detailed in <i>the</i> <i>Book of Chantries,</i> is listed as Dreamspeaker Barabbus, despite being raised by a cult to be a Nephandus.<br /> <br /> The Jade Demon, also described in <i>the</i> <i>Book of Chantries</i>, is described as betraying his 'Dark Lords', breaking his pact with them and surviving. This is contradictory to the writing that says that Nephandus can't go back on being a Nephandus.<br /> Despite The Jade Demon breaking his pact, he is still listed as a Nephandus; and a True Mage serving him is listed as a Barabbus.<br /> <br /> Non-Nephandi True Mages who are regularly interacting with the Nephandi - sometimes due to threats - are listed as being Barabbi of their respective Traditions in<i> the </i><i>Book of Chantries</i>.<br /> <br /> Two of the three of the original Nephandi factions - the K'llashaa and the Malfean Nephandi - are described as &quot;being thought as being too unstable by the other Nephandi&quot;...It's hard to think that they would have the opinnion of being unstable if they aren't the minority. I guess this is what the Infernal Nephandi think of the other two factions?<br /> <br /> The majority of the Nephandi are described as knowing Pictish to communicate with the Black Spiral Dancers...I dunno, just feels and seems too far-fetched.<br /> <br /> <i>The Book of Madness </i>2nd edition says that the Nephandi Patrons might actually be nightmares of the sleeping Neverborn (from <i>Wraith: The Oblivion</i>) . This seems senseless, and is contradictory to other material.<br /> <br /> The Seers of the Throne \u2013 or going by Mage: The Ascension, the Traditions and the Technocracy - care not about this propaganda of lies being tangled with senselessness; after all, in their view point the 'upstart' Nephandi will be defeated soon...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1141032#post1141032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why the &quot;evil&quot; or bad label seems so non-sense, it's just military propaganda, since when did universal morality and ethics mattered to reality bending humans? Who watch the watchers?</div> </div> </div> </div>At it's simplest, I see the Nephandi as True Mages who \u2013 unlike the Traditions or the Technocracy \u2013 have absolutely no illusions that you have to Awaken every single Sleeper as some kind of lofty goal. And some of the Sleepers / mundane humans have to be killed, of course. Maybe lots of them. And the Traditions - and others - call this outlook 'Descension'.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi are also unafraid to make pacts with entities that can be regarded as dark and/or alien, and to delve into areas of Magick such as demonology. This makes them hated by the Traditions and the Technocrats \u2013 and by the Order of Reason - and by most other True Mages. This is largely due to lack of understanding, superstitions, and jealousy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-17-2017, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T09:39:33-07:00","id":1141095,"title":"","content":"Nephandi apologists are somewhat amazing.<br /> <br /> There are things that, currently, to us, our time and our culture are not okay. Some of them are weird. Killing lots of people in an action-adventure sense is much more okay than, say, showing people having sex. But there are MANY things that are deep, serious taboos: cannibalism, incest, slavery are a few outstanding examples, but there are reasons that those and other topics that are repeatedly called out with trigger warnings in the source books. They are things that, on a gut level, our society and culture think are just plain BAD. Sure, they may not have always been. And they may not be now to particular groups, but, in general, people who are okay with them are effectively othered with extreme prejudice. For example, it's just not okay to eat other people (even though cannibalism has ranged from being common practice to a religious sacrament depending on time and place). <br /> <br /> That seems to be the intent behind the Nephandi as a group. They the things that exist and the things that people do that aren't just not okay, they're fundamentally abhorrent to us (here and now). They are that personified, like the Marauders, Technocracy, Traditions and Disparates (the last two being close to the same thing with different emphasis) are personifications of their own things.<br /> <br /> It's easy to try to make backflips to justify Nephandi as something basic or fundamental or the &quot;guys who really know the TRUTH&quot;, but it's largely sophistry. It's trying to redefine the inherently immoral as moral. It's trying to prove that negative is positive. I mean, look how the arguments usually go... Starts with: &quot;There is no objective truth/right or wrong....&quot;. Ends with &quot;The Nephandi are the ones who know the TRUTH and are the ones who are right, while everyone else is wrong.&quot; <br /> <br /> Genuine evil qua evil in the here and now is a very abstract concept until and unless you face it. Spending time at a murder scene or having the occasion to talk to a serial killer and the Nephandi don't really seem all that hard a concept to grasp. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T09:58:49-07:00","id":1141100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1141095#post1141095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems to be the intent behind the Nephandi as a group. They the things that exist and the things that people do that aren't just not okay, they're fundamentally abhorrent to us (here and now).</div> </div> </div> </div>From which M:tA material - which parts of the books - specifically did you get this idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-17-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T11:23:25-07:00","id":1141137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1141095#post1141095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they're fundamentally abhorrent to us (here and now).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eliminating people out of existence based on something they were born with, outside their control, hypothetical or not, seems abhorrent to me and akin to the religious rationale iberians came up with to justify slavery during the exploration/colonization age: black people are born without a soul, thus even if they convert, they can't fix themselves. Or for example, the indian caste system: people are born dalits, untouchable, and they can't change that.<br /> <br /> I'm not a nephandi apologist to be honest. They just seem contradictory; the inverted avatar is a constant unhampered by death and irreversible, yet we don't see nephandi controlling the world, we don't actually see any nephandi damage on reality. Are they really evil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:46:25-07:00","id":1141190,"title":"","content":"Nephandi.... People who hunt children, do unspeakable things to them (I mean, I COULD speak of it, but it's the sort of thing that would justifiably get someone kicked off the board), skin and eat them while they are still alive, all while filming it and posting it live on social media after having incentivized it properly to make certain their [arents/caretakers would be forced to watch. (Which wouldn't be very hard at all... The first episode of Black Mirror is a good example of those kind of tactics) Oh, and let's film the parents too, and have a sort of reverse PSA that reminds every parent and child out there that this is completely random and they could very well be next. Kinda like the absolute and total reverse of every &quot;save this poor animal&quot; or &quot;help out this starving child&quot; ad ever. A plan that, overall, would probably make Giles de Rais giggle.<br /> <br /> Defend them. Without ignoring each and every bit of what I was saying about &quot;here and now&quot; and &quot;our culture&quot;. <br /> <br /> I don't need to cite pages in M20 or Book of Secrets. It's actually kinda hard NOT to trip over the altercasting. <br /> <br /> And we DO see Nephandi damage on the world. It's the WoD. It's Nephandi damaged all over. There's all sorts of historical legerdemain in the canon that demonstrates the effects Nephandi have had. It seems just plain bizarre to trot out many of the things that are at least partially attributed to Nephandic influence (the horrors of colonialism and slavery, genocide, the meat-grinder sort of warfare from from WWI onwards, etc.) as a defense against mistreating &quot;poor misunderstood Nephandi&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:57:23-07:00","id":1141197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1141137#post1141137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eliminating people out of existence based on something they were born with, outside their control, hypothetical or not, seems abhorrent to me and akin to the religious rationale iberians came up with to justify slavery during the exploration/colonization age: black people are born without a soul, thus even if they convert, they can't fix themselves. Or for example, the indian caste system: people are born dalits, untouchable, and they can't change that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is whether the feature they were born with actually meaningfully predicts their behavior or not. Consider Blood Brothers (<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Blood_Brothers\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Blood_Brothers</a>). They had no choice in their creation, but they are little more than murder machines for their masters. It's not their fault, but they still need to be destroyed by those who seek peace. Their state not being their choice or their fault merely means their destruction is not punishment. Compare to Indian castes, where one's caste says nothing about whether you will kill hundreds of people in your life or not.<br /> <br /> Let's assume widderslainte were 100% guaranteed to spend their life murdering and torturing hundreds of people. No ifs, ands, or buts. Would you still refuse to kill or Gilgul one if you had the opportunity, solely because their status as a murder machine was not due to their conscious choice?<br /> <br /> If you'd be willing to do so in that case, then it's merely a question of at what percentage you'd no longer be willing to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T16:37:48-07:00","id":1141250,"title":"","content":"From a mage political point of view, nephandi are poor and misunderstood. Every faction has more or less a window of action. The technocracy hates the traditions but are known to engage in dialogue with them or even cooperate with them in face of larger threats. The traditions see disparates as misguided by accepted fellows. Meanwhile we never get the nephandi point of view, just external perceptions about them. At first they want to destroy the world, then they are responsible for the world corruption, suffering and pain? Or are they judeo-christian infernalists shoehorned into a Unknown Armies/Matrix setting?<br /> <br /> Comparing them with blood brothers is incoherent, they aren't an experiment, a bizarre project, they are- or should be- rational agents with long term strategical objectives.<br /> <br /> When Senex claims to have cured Amanda of her inverted avatar, what guarantees we have that he isn't a snake oil seller in 19th century wild west, calling a hired actor from the crowd to cure an invented illness and sell his miraculous product?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T19:35:52-07:00","id":1141284,"title":"","content":"None. Exactly Zero. Except that is in no way the narrative. It's engaging in a number of logical fallacies to stack up a contra-factual argument that goes against the fundamentals of the faction as described in the book. &quot;Redeeming a Nephandi&quot; is only snake-oil if you re-jigger the argument to making Nephandi-dom something that one doesn't have to be saved from. (Hence, Nephandi apologist/)<br /> <br /> The thing is that the Nephandi aren't really a political faction in the same way the Traditions, Technocracy, or Disparates. So making political arguments about their motivations as if they were the same is, once again, sophistry. Nephandi are like the Marauders. They are fundamentally changed away from your core points. Comparing them (particularly the Widderslainte) to the Blood Brotehrs isn't incoherent, it's a good analogy. (I guess the other Nephandi would be like someone who chose to be a Blood Brother if you extend the analogy). They fundamentally aren't (completely)rational actors. They may walk and talk like them (unlike the vast majority of the Marauders) but they don't have the same range of choices. They can't choose to be not-Nephandi anymore than someone with a life-threatening illness can choose to not be sick anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 09-18-2017, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T20:10:21-07:00","id":1141294,"title":"","content":"I agree with Ajax. While it would be all well and good to argue about a version of the Nephandi that are a persecuted, misunderstood minority, that is not a version of the Nephandi that is supported seriously in any Mage: The Ascension text. We have no alternative to the idea of the Nephandi being categorically evil presented in the 20+ years of material printed about them. If that seems one-sided and weird, I don't know what to tell you. Except that this is how it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, I want to challenge the proposition that targeting Widderslainte for termination is morally wrong. Not because I don't agree that it is bad. But I see it less as &quot;reprehensible&quot;, and more &quot;unfortunate&quot;. Regardless of whether a Widderslainte can truly be seen as responsible for their evil actions, they still engage in evil actions. Indeed, the fact that they can't choose NOT to be evil makes it all the more important that they be eliminated. To paraphrase Isaac Asimov's robot novels, a Nephandus is Logical, but not Reasonable. Which is to say, they may have the ability to think abstractly and plan and other things Sapient beings do, but they do so according to value judgments completely antithetical to the values of humans. It just &quot;feels right&quot; to a Nephandus - and especially to a Widderslainte - to do evil things.<br /> <br /> When you have a being like that, their responsibility for their actions - or lack thereof - becomes a moot point. They NEED to be taken care of, because they don't play nice with the rest of humanity. They are a threat, and bald, simple pragmatism cannot permit them to run unchecked. Any more than one can reasonably allow a rabid, angry dog to run in the streets. It's the same reason I personally advocate the Joker be executed, if not by Batman then by the state. He may be too mad to truly be responsible for his actions, but his actions are uncontrollable, uncontainable, and unconscionable nonetheless. After a certain point - after the Joker has escaped Arkham and gone on a killing spree for the 100th time - you just have to throw up your hands and say, &quot;The clown can't be cured, and is too dangerous to be left alive&quot;. I'm surprised an angry mob in Gotham never tried to rip him from a squad car and string him up from a lamp post, because they were simply sick of dealing with him.<br /> <br /> With the Nephandi, it's the same, but on the scale of entire factions. You don't think regular Mages have tried to reform the Nephandi? That they haven't attempted to listen to their side of the story? The Fallen have been a thorn in the sides of the Awakened for thousands of years. The other factions don't call for the Fallen to be annihilated because they've rushed to a prejudiced judgment. They call for their destruction because they've been burned ALL THE TIMES, and have given up trying. <br /> <br /> Fool me once, shame on me. Fool me for thousands of years, I'm fairly comfortable shooting you on sight. While morality may demand that one keep trying to save someone until it gets done, people are weak, and have only so much patience. And all of this while the Nephandi have spent every waking moment doing horrible things, consorting with Actual Demons from Actual Hell (and other places), and trying to get good people to go bad.<br /> <br /> Even if the Nephandi ARE misunderstood, surely you can forgive the rest of Mage-kind for thinking otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T08:47:37-07:00","id":1141419,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But you're forgetting that ALL THE MAGE MATERIAL EVER WRITTEN was created by the evil Traditions and Technocracy to marginalize the good and misunderstood Nephandi. NOTHING written about nephandi it's true unless it agrees with what Muad'Dib and visigoth believe (which means that nothing ever written it's true). Surely you can't believe that Widderslainte would do anything evil because all those lies that were written about them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7219_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7219\" data-vbnamecard=\"7219\">visigoth</a><br /> Now that I think about it, because ALL THE MAGE MATERIAL EVER WRITTEN it's Technotraditionalist propaganda...<b>how do we know Nephandi EXIST</b>: Maybe they're a boogeyman invented to explain the excesses and bad deeds of the Masters. What, you think Pentex is evil?...well it's not that we, the Syndicate, are evil, but merely a typical case of Nepandi infiltration. Why we couldn't predict or stop the Nazi?, they had Nephandi working for them! . If you think otherwise, surely you're a Nephandi. Obviously if Nephandi weren't evil they would already used their reality warping + the power of their masters to clrear this misunderstanding, so, the only logical conclusion it's that Nephandi do not exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-18-2017, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T09:21:26-07:00","id":1141427,"title":"","content":"i don't think this is up for debate or anything, i mean it can be...<br /> but unless u explain exactly to me what is the rational and wise aspect in killing and skinning alive women and children and use rape and torture as focus, while u take advantage of innocent people and spread entropy and objective corruption through the universe, then there is no point.<br /> <br /> try exactly yo explain how that should be a justifiable mean to knowledge or salvation or... ascension? without sounding like a serial killer, Charles Manson on lsd or an outright lunatic.<br /> Sophistry and manipulation of language can get you only so far, as human beings we know better or less that some things are just plain... wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:03:56-07:00","id":1141959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1141419#post1141419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think about it, because ALL THE MAGE MATERIAL EVER WRITTEN it's Technotraditionalist propaganda...</div> </div> </div> </div>But it really is. You never asked yourself why tradition spheres seem like a copy pasted version of the hermetic-kaballistic tree of life? Why the avatar is only the roman-greek concept of genius, a convoluted guardian angel? Why the pogroms suddenly halted even though the technocracy is the hegemonic power with all resources at hand? Why traditions adopt peripheral, heterodox, or polemic worldviews in western society, as if ignoring the world's reality of power? Why they pursue the social darwinism and positivism of ascension?<br /> The highest probability is that traditions and magic as a whole is a technocratic experiment. A controlled albeit ignorant group of psionics. A manchurian candidate inserted to solve finally the vampire and werewolf question. A bug tracking system to the technocracy ethics, never allowed outside of its specific function and ignorant of everything else. A psychiatric experiment, they are all mad and believe they can bend reality (but still hunt judeo-christian devil worshipper hallucinations due to a childhood trauma).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:48:30-07:00","id":1141984,"title":"","content":"Or it isn't because that's not the narrative. I guess, I mean, it could be if you want it to be. If you have a group of players who enjoy that sort of game.... But to assert and aver that that's the game proper? Balderdash.<br /> <br /> The Spheres are a game mechanic that exists both above and on the table. So it has to be reflected in some way that makes sense to all the various groups across the board. Oh, and from fluff-land, it's a system that seems to be an accurate description in game of the fundamentals of the way reality actually works, so, when whoever sussed it out (I'm sure the Hermetics will take credit for it and/or the nabobs of the nascent Order of Reason) it spread like wildfire. Because it works (sotto voice &quot;Because it's the rules&quot;). <br /> <br /> The Avatar is a game mechanic, so it's got to be explainable somehow in a way that makes sense across the board. Even if it doesn't really make sense, it has to make sense enough because pretty much every Mage has the Background. After that, it can be anything from a Platonic daimon to your pet cat to the Voice of God to the static on the TV to bumblebees (as a concept). That's not Roman nor Greek nor Romano-Greek (nor Platonic nor Aristotelian etc.) <br /> <br /> The Union is not the hegemonic power with all the resources and never has been. (But they are insanely delighted that you think they are.) There aren't enough of them to do more than nudge and instigate. <br /> <br /> The Pogrom hasn't been a constant. It has waxed and waned since the Union was founded (and the Order). <br /> <br /> The Traditions have been having internal conflict over the ideologies and culture and magical praxes of the world from the get-go. The small group that started the Traditions came from Western Europe (like, utlimately the people who wrote the game) and they recruited outsiders, but it was still largely their clubhouse and their rules. And that has been a categorical weakness from the get go (by excluding groups, driving groups away, mashing groups together that didn't fit well). But as much as they have been overshadowed by Western thought, there has been a counter-current of ecumenicism and inclusiveness that flows in the other direction too. <br /> <br /> Social Darwinism is inherently about position. In that one's position is proof of one's fitness. (It's really really bad misunderstanding of the fundamentals of the concept as part of Darwin's Theory of Evolution... but oh well). Since pretty much every mage starts out as an Orphan who erupts, there isn't as much of a possibility of &quot;good breeding&quot; and prior placement mattering. Sure it may pop up and there is definitely going to be some gladhanding and party favors passed out. But the recruitment pool is &quot;All of Humanity&quot; and there's no knowing where the next potential will come from. That's pretty much inherently the opposite of Social Darwinism... The &quot;best&quot; people don't become mages. Anyone can become a mage. And there's bugger-all way to pass down excellence. <br /> <br /> The highest probability is that the game is what it says it is and the game world, while rich with secrets and contradictions and unexplained nooks and crannies, is pretty much exactly what it presents itself as. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:51:26-07:00","id":1141985,"title":"","content":"And Nephandi aren't secretly the good guys. <br /> <br /> Maybe if you were making the case the Marauders were, within the confines of the games internal teleology you might get some traction. But the Nephandi... No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T08:31:46-07:00","id":1142165,"title":"","content":"The Nephandi can't be the good guys if there's no right or wrong in the world because, if they can't be evil because evil itself it's a concept fabricated by the Technotraditionalist conspiration, then they can't be good either because these are logical opposites, one can't be defined without defining the other as it's opposition<br /> <br /> And they certainly can't be the good guys if they are anything like the book says they are because no current moral compass can condone what they're supposed to do (their means AND ends at the same time).<br /> <br /> Thus, the only logical option once you've discarded Nephandi being evil it's that <i>Nephandi do not exist</i>.<br /> <br /> But Nephandi being good, <b><i>never</i></b>. If they exist as anything more than a smokescreen, they're evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it really is. You never asked yourself why tradition spheres seem like a copy pasted version of the hermetic-kaballistic tree of life? Why the avatar is only the roman-greek concept of genius, a convoluted guardian angel? Why the pogroms suddenly halted even though the technocracy is the hegemonic power with all resources at hand? Why traditions adopt peripheral, heterodox, or polemic worldviews in western society, as if ignoring the world's reality of power? Why they pursue the social darwinism and positivism of ascension?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a setting, one where everything in the books, even things like the Spheres, Arete, Avatar, was written by the Technotraditionalist conspiracy (the only one where Nephandi can not be evil, by virtue of not existing), it's not supported. Think that Spheres, Paradox, and so on, are being doubted. Thus, the very system of the game it's false. To follow this idea to it's extreme you should discard the Spheres and use other rules for everything, have another story and metaplot.<i> At that point you're not playing Mage: The Ascencion anymore.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The highest probability is that the game is what it says it is and the game world, while rich with secrets and contradictions and unexplained nooks and crannies, is pretty much exactly what it presents itself as.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> One has to have a very peculiar world view to think the authors of a RPG would purposely lie about its rules and story.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that if I were to ask Satyros if the Nephandi are evil, and he said <i>yes</i>, visigoth won't be satisfied because obviously the author it's part of the conspiracy to hide the truth about Nephandi <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Illuminatus confirmed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-20-2017, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T10:02:19-07:00","id":1142194,"title":"","content":"The Nephandi serve in game to provide a 'these are evil guys you can wail on without worrying about whether you are evil for hurting humans' role. Also, the talk of descent and the inverted Avatar is a dark mirror and allows the use of demonic pact tropes.<br /> <br /> As for RPG authors, I can imagine them lying about parts of a story in a conspiratorial type game such as Mage. Part of a story with many perspectives is that truth is very much in the eyes of the beholder and RPG fans can press for many details, so at times I could believe an author misdirected the audience so they didn't reveal major plot. A good TV show example of a narrator who lies or is at least unreliable is <i>Mr. Robot</i>.<br /> <br /> I plan on letting my players smack down the Nephandi without moral qualms, though there could be social and legal qualms for their PCs that lead to other moral qualms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T10:46:41-07:00","id":1142215,"title":"","content":"Though it's not fun to be reminded of this - Mage: the Ascension is simply a set of roleplaying books. The world it describes only exists as far as its writers wrote. If somebody asks &quot;Hey, what was Porthos doing in the Deep Umbra after WW2?&quot; there is no answer because nobody wrote it down and published it.<br /> <br /> If you think it would be cool in <i>your</i> game to have a specific answer to that question (&quot;He was punching the Wyrm in the nads!&quot; &quot;He made Grandmother a cake made out of Forces!&quot;), that's great, but you have to get your players to agree to fork off a new game setting in that way. Rather than modifying the published setting, you are creating a derivative setting in your head and copying it into the heads of your friends.<br /> <br /> So if you want to create your own version of Mage: the Ascension where Nephandi are somehow the good guys for eating babies and making grimoires out of their flayed skin, and the Technocracy runs the Traditions as controlled opposition, that's fine, and good luck convincing your friends to play your custom game with you. But you cannot change the <i>published</i> setting because you aren't writing those books. If the books say Avatars are guardian angels, that the Spheres are pulled right from Kabbalism, etc. - then that is the objective truth of the game.<br /> <br /> And if the books say that Nephandi are irredeemably evil, that nobody comes back from Avatar inversion unless an archmaster takes a personal interest and maybe not even then - then that is the objective truth of the setting.<br /> <br /> If you're going to claim the <i>entirety</i> of the books are in-character chatter from universally unreliable narrators - where do you draw the line? Is the character sheet also propaganda? What about the table of contents? Does Phil Brucato <i>even exist</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7356,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","user":"haldir2012","date":". 09-20-2017, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T12:43:07-07:00","id":1142267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142215#post1142215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to claim the <i>entirety</i> of the books are in-character chatter from universally unreliable narrators - where do you draw the line? Is the character sheet also propaganda? What about the table of contents? <b>Does Phil Brucato <i>even exist</i></b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I laughed so hard at that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T13:49:44-07:00","id":1142291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142165#post1142165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure that if I were to ask Satyros if the Nephandi are evil, and he said <i>yes</i>, visigoth won't be satisfied because obviously the author it's part of the conspiracy to hide the truth about Nephandi <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Illuminatus confirmed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What would he say to me if I asked him the nephandi internal logic? I buy what Ajax said about nephandi being more like marauders than a rational faction, but this is never expressed in the books.<br /> <br /> Also, the same author who decided Lions of Zion are out of the game due to his political subjective views, and who, in my opinion, doesn't have the monopoly on mage.<br /> <br /> Of course I was joking when I said the previous conspiracy theory, but I'm surprised people don't agree that there is a striking lack of consistency regarding nephandi, not even about the abyssal lords they serve, specially when considering how game breaking, how mechanics breaking is an inverted avatar. Ok, they are evil. But what are their internal logic?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T16:38:13-07:00","id":1142336,"title":"","content":"How does it break any mechanics at all? In any meaningful way? Qlippothic Spheres are pretty much just the same Spheres with &quot;eeeeeeeeevil&quot; loosely (lamely) attached. The Techno Alt-Spheres are more different (and not broken).<br /> <br /> The Marauders are bit broken with their powerful Quiets, but not in an entirely bad way. IF (caps intended) there was some actual mechanic like Quiet for the Nephandi, that actually might solve a lot of these problems. Then there would be something to point at to demonstrate the &quot;broken&quot; aspects of the &quot;broken&quot; Factions of mages. Then there would be something to point at to say &quot;That's the manifestation of their internal logic.&quot; (Which would give us slightly different things to argue about.)<br /> <br /> I dunno, I might just break down and go with Dreamweaver and say that there are three flavors of mages that have lost it and they track the three different kids of Quiet. Marauders, Nephandi (for the Jhor) and some really hard ass Pattern types (anit-mages? Skeptics? The Clarified?)<br /> <br /> I can see not putting in the Lions of Zion for the obvious reasons vis-a-vis the name and the obvious gross misunderstandings it raises, but, sheesh, it wouldn't be too hard to find something else to call them (something more historically and mystically accurate even) and throw them in with the Disparates (and Traditions, like all the other Disparate Faction with their Tradition analogue/defector/spies bretheren). Of course, Brucato also says mage CAN'T be a city-based/location-based game. Which is complete folderol and is completely belied by the fact that most of the Backgrounds are difficult to impossible to effectively utilize in most other settings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T04:00:34-07:00","id":1142453,"title":"","content":"The problem is with viewing the Nephandi as a &quot;Faction&quot; like they are a Tradition or Convention. They are not. They have Cabals that work towards whichever twisted vision they have but are hardly a unified front of any flavour. <br /> <br /> The internal logic varies from Nephandus to Nephandus but they are all walking, willing servants of Nihilistic forces. For some examples look at the Joker from Batman. Or if you want to get chills how about the first couple of seasons if Once Upon A Time, only Henry is a Nephandus and everything else is his influence on the town of Storybrooke for his own needs. Go on think about it. The Nephandi want the world to burn, they want it to rot, they want it to suffer and why? Because maybe its better to rule in hell than serve in heaven? Maybe the suffering of others in some way lessens their pain or it brings them a twisted joy? Maybe they want it their way and who cares what the cost to the rest of the world is? Or what is left in the wake of the Nephandus ambition? <br /> <br /> Why do people do the petty and cruel things they do? What happens when the worst of humanity gain the keys to reality? That's a Nephandus. Marauders are terrifyingly mad trapped in their own reality. Nephandi are the madness if Reality walking around inside it. <br /> <br /> Another good example is Konrad Kurze in the Horus Heresy series. He's totally Nephandus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T08:03:56-07:00","id":1142515,"title":"","content":"My two cents on Nephandi motivations:<br /> <br /> An inverted Avatar means that they feel satisfied, happy, accomplished, and all that when they hurt, break down, or mar something. The warm fuzzies other people get from helping, they instead get from hurting. Imagine if someone got a shock to the pleasure center of their brain - or more reasonably, an injection of heroin - when they harmed.<br /> <br /> On top of that, for <i>barrabi</i> or <i>widderslainte</i> who have Awakened, that inverted Avatar speaks to them. Rather than being pushed to perfection, Ascension, and self-improvement, they are pushed to ruin, to mar, and to break down. They quite literally have a devil on their shoulder.<br /> <br /> Therefore, it's nonsensical to propose rehabilitating a Nephandus. Could you tell a normal person, &quot;You must never help another person. You must never love someone else. You must never build something or leave a legacy&quot;? Of course not. They might be coerced into behaving that way temporarily but they will be inexorably pulled to the direction their heart truly lies. The Nephandus is the same way - he or she cannot deny that their heart is in it when they do evil, and it will always be so. They cannot deny who they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T08:24:28-07:00","id":1142529,"title":"","content":"Those comparing Nephandi to Marauders are not mistaken. In many ways they are opposite sides of the same coin. The Marauders incoherent and fragmented, but you can see some of how their mind works as they change the world around you. The Nephandi coherent and intentional, but you can never get a glimpse of their alien thought processes. The Technocracy and the Traditions are examples of where human thinking can take you. Nephandi and Marauders are examples of what the influence of the Avatar can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T09:18:48-07:00","id":1142552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142291#post1142291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course I was joking when I said the previous conspiracy theory, but I'm surprised people don't agree that there is a striking lack of consistency regarding nephandi, not even about the abyssal lords they serve, specially when considering how game breaking, how mechanics breaking is an inverted avatar. Ok, they are evil. But what are their internal logic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage has so many contradictions (like, everywhere) that I'm accustomed to it. In fact, I think it's part of it's &quot;charm&quot;, if that makes sense. You can choose to side with a fully consensual reality or one where a few things aren't consensual, for instance. But everything has a limit, when nothing goes your way there's no place to choose. <br /> <br /> In first edition the game worked on a Reality that was surprisingly objective: All mage factions but the Traditions aligned towards a member of the Methaphysical Trinity, exept of the Traditions that represented the force of balance. Nephandi internal logic was that they were &quot;Wyrm&quot; mages. Nephandi, Technocrats and Marauders were all deemed evil because they were &quot;unbalanced&quot;, the Trinity needs to be balanced for the universe to exist, but the Nephandi were pushing for their side with exclusion of the others (and also were evil becuase the Wyrm it's corrupt and all that Werewolf has to say about that). <br /> <br /> Of course, that isn't the case anymore, Technocracy it's fully good (or as good as the Trads) throwing the 1rst edition methaphysics out the window, but as you can see there's a logic in saying that Nephandi are insane like Marauders. In first edition they <i>were.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T10:22:11-07:00","id":1142583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142529#post1142529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those comparing Nephandi to Marauders are not mistaken. In many ways they are opposite sides of the same coin.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are almost literally the opposite sides of the same coin. There is a reason why Marauders almost always attack Nephandi on sight, and are downright hunting them with more zealotry than the Traditions ever will. If you want to cause *real* trouble for the Nephandi, somehow manage to point a bunch of Marauders at their lair and then get far far away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T11:49:13-07:00","id":1142627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142583#post1142583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are almost literally the opposite sides of the same coin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going with this, what would you call the coin itself?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1141294#post1141294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't think regular Mages have tried to reform the Nephandi? That they haven't attempted to listen to their side of the story?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't seem so at all to me. Have you read anything in World of Darkness that says or suggests otherwise?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1141294#post1141294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if the Nephandi ARE misunderstood, surely you can forgive the rest of Mage-kind for thinking otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it could be forgiven, but I think and feel it definitely shouldn't be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1141250#post1141250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Senex claims to have cured Amanda of her inverted avatar, what guarantees we have that he isn't a snake oil seller in 19th century wild west, calling a hired actor from the crowd to cure an invented illness and sell his miraculous product?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is much worse than this. Considering Senex is a member of the Euthanatoi, he is the True Mage equivalent of a snake oil salesman with a group of very dangerous and possibly hostile thugs standing next to him - threatening anyone who speaks against his peddling of the snake oil, and also threatening those that don't want to buy the snake oil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-21-2017, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T12:10:14-07:00","id":1142643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't seem so at all to me. Have you read anything in World of Darkness that says or suggests otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty much stated that this was and often is the case and that it always ends bad. Just read the book of madness taking out your conspiration lenses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> threatening anyone who speaks against the snake oil he tries to peddle, and also threatening those that don't want to buy the snake oil. </div> </div> </div>Senex does this each time someone says Amanda it's still a Nephandi and should be Gilguled. But why would he do a &quot;fake&quot; cure?, He's an Archmaster and the leader of a whole Tradition, he has all the power and prestige in the universe, what's the motivation?, what can he gain that he hasn't already?. If there's nothing to &quot;cure&quot; then obviously anyone on the power level to even matter to Senex would know about the ruse because no one would be able to prevent them from knowing. When you know how MASSIVELY powerful it's Senex the only reason to fake this would be to please his own stubbornness, to not admit that Nephandi can't be cured (as it goes against Good Death premises).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-21-2017, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T12:28:49-07:00","id":1142650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142627#post1142627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going with this, what would you call the coin itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chaos.<br /> The Marauders are agents of what you'd call the Wyld in MTA. Chaos personified. A chaos that stands for uncontrolled creation and change.<br /> The Nephandi are chaos as well. Entropic chaos meant to end everything - the opposite of creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T20:52:03-07:00","id":1142804,"title":"","content":"I can understand the frustration with the Nephandi being portrayed as exemplars of absolute evil. After all, the Technocracy went from being exemplars of absolute oppression to something more nuanced as the editions advanced and more supplemental material came out. It is a world defined by subjectivity. That's why I think &quot;evil&quot; is--while largely accurate--not the best way to describe the Nephandi. &quot;Destructive&quot; is a more useful concept that goes past subjective judgment. It also leaves room for more complexity, because they need to have reasons for why they want to destroy.<br /> <br /> Some possible Nephandic arguments for destroying everything (not all are mutually compatible):<br /> <br /> -The inertia of our reality is too much to overcome without completely destroying it; its very physicality overshadows the spiritual and any chance of collective Ascension.<br /> -Suffering and futility are ubiquitous. Nephandic foci are horrific but show reality for what it is, and (they believe) are the only way to transcend it.<br /> -Reality as we experience it is a collective illusion defined by the lowest common denominator.<br /> <br /> They still need to be stopped. But at least this way of looking at them makes more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T23:33:12-07:00","id":1142818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142804#post1142804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand the frustration with the Nephandi being portrayed as exemplars of absolute evil. After all, the Technocracy went from being exemplars of absolute oppression to something more nuanced as the editions advanced and more supplemental material came out. It is a world defined by subjectivity. That's why I think &quot;evil&quot; is--while largely accurate--not the best way to describe the Nephandi. &quot;Destructive&quot; is a more useful concept that goes past subjective judgment. It also leaves room for more complexity, because they need to have reasons for why they want to destroy.<br /> <br /> Some possible Nephandic arguments for destroying everything (not all are mutually compatible):<br /> <br /> -The inertia of our reality is too much to overcome without completely destroying it; its very physicality overshadows the spiritual and any chance of collective Ascension.<br /> -Suffering and futility are ubiquitous. Nephandic foci are horrific but show reality for what it is, and (they believe) are the only way to transcend it.<br /> -Reality as we experience it is a collective illusion defined by the lowest common denominator.<br /> <br /> They still need to be stopped. But at least this way of looking at them makes more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where you and I differ. You say that making the Nephandi about Destruction makes them make more sense...and then say this is a good thing.<br /> <br /> I disagree. I think the Nephandi's motivation making sense is counter to how I prefer them: Evil because their motivations are antithetical to what reasonable people want.<br /> <br /> You're free to run the Nephandi however you choose, but I prefer the Nephandi representing Evil that is not only absolute, but senseless. It makes their atrocities all the more horrible, as they serve no purpose, ultimately, than to be done for their own sake. I like my Nephandi to see Atrocity, not as a means to an end, but the End unto itself.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that they aren't just driven towards destruction. That they aren't just to the Wyrm what the Maruaders are to the Wyld. Hedging exactly to the trinity from WtA is more limiting than what they could otherwise be.<br /> <br /> For me, the Nephandi are best when they are fundamentally broken. All arguments stated in your post being not the reasons why Nephandi do what they do, but after-the-fact rationalizations for the atrocities and destruction they would do anyway. All their complex webs of philosophy - whether they believe it or simply feed it to potential converts - being attempts to justify with logic the urge to wreck and ruin they feel, which is inherently illogical (and, indeed, counter-logical for a social organism like humans).<br /> <br /> Indeed, I want to see a Nephandus who actively works to counter the end-of-the-world plans other Nephandi make. Not out of the goodness in his heart - that doesn't exist, and he only pretends otherwise when he's trying to deceive someone. Rather, he fights to prevent the apocalypse...so his fun doesn't stop. He doesn't like to destroy...just to make people suffer. It's entirely gratifying to him to personally be the fly in the world's ointment, allowing folks to have otherwise good lives, so it'll hurt more when he comes in to ruin them with torture, rape, etc.<br /> <br /> He hurts people, and wants to <i>go on</i> hurting people. And if his fellow Fallen want to end his fun, that just means they are valid targets for his enjoyment.<br /> <br /> If the Nephandi only represented Destruction in the same way the Marauders represented Chaos, you couldn't have a character like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T04:11:24-07:00","id":1142851,"title":"","content":"If you want a Nephandi who wants to destroy everything but is still convincing or alluring, consider Morpheus in The Matrix. From the perspective of someone in the Matrix, he is terrible: he regularly and casually kills people and destroys buildings, and on top of that, he'll gladly explain that these are merely tools for his eventual goal of destroying the reality in which you're living. <br /> <br /> What if the movie was different after Neo took the red pill? What if they never actually &quot;unplugged&quot; and instead stayed in that reality, engaging in mass killing so they ruined the machines' crops from the inside? And there was never objective validation of Morpheus's claims?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T07:29:08-07:00","id":1142895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand the frustration with the Nephandi being portrayed as exemplars of absolute evil. After all, the Technocracy went from being exemplars of absolute oppression to something more nuanced as the editions advanced and more supplemental material came out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. Nephandi can be a lot cartoonish, sometimes I wonder how they manage to infiltrate anyone. I can see why someone would want to make them more complex<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is a world defined by subjectivity. </div> </div> </div>But this is just lazy. &quot;I'm not evil because I believe I'm not evil&quot;?. You need to elaborate how this &quot;subjetive reality&quot; unveils itself if you want to convince anyone. How this belief actually 'warps' reality in ways that people could understand as &quot;not evil&quot;. Otherwise you don't have non-cartoonish villans, but the villans of the Carebears (well, maybe that was what you were aiming for <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> btw, Mage isn't based on subjectivism but relativism. Reality it's only subjective for Marauders, otherwise it's Consensual. You don't see Marauders trying to convince people about their reality because they litteraly live in a bubble, but other mages don't, they know they need to fight if they don't want their ways to be lost. There may be even trully objective things thrown there. Mage it's very contradictory about how much reality depends on humans, but it has ever been very adamant about the collective will of humans mattering more than the individual will of mages, to the point where trying to control this will makes sense for mages<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why I think &quot;evil&quot; is--while largely accurate--not the best way to describe the Nephandi. &quot;Destructive&quot; is a more useful concept that goes past subjective judgment. </div> </div> </div>I disagree on principle. The only thing about Nephandi that can be called &quot;destructive&quot; it's their end goal, but that's not what they <i>do</i>. Destructive means to cause damage and break stuff, a bomb it's destructive, a Flambeau mage it's destructive, a Terrorist it's destructive. Nephandi flying people alive with glee aren't being &quot;destructive&quot;, the purpose it's not to kill or hurt the person, but to cause suffering. Nephandi do search for the ultimate destruction, but that's their &quot;lofty abstract ideal&quot;, so to speak, it's what they <i>do</i> more than their end goals what makes the evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -The inertia of our reality is too much to overcome without completely destroying it; its very physicality overshadows the spiritual and any chance of collective Ascension. </div> </div> </div>This it's what they say, as per the Book of Madness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Suffering and futility are ubiquitous. Nephandic foci are horrific but show reality for what it is, and (they believe) are the only way to transcend it.<br /> -Reality as we experience it is a collective illusion defined by the lowest common denominator. </div> </div> </div>This isn't what they say.<br /> <br /> There are mage factions, like the Aghori, that believe this and aren't Nephandi. BTW, the Aghori are evil, they do evil knowing that it's evil (it's not a case of bule/orange morality, they do evil BECAUSE it's Evil. They won't do it if they didn't believed it was evil) to trascend the ilusion of this world. That makes them evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They still need to be stopped. But at least this way of looking at them makes more sense. </div> </div> </div>Again, &quot;them being destructive&quot; it's an horrendous reason to kill Nephandi. Flambeau are destructive and you don't see them being persecuted. Aghori aren't very destructive (they torture to teach Ascencion), but evil, and the Extatics wage an internal war against them (and have presented a motion to declare them barabbi, a term normaly reserved for Nephandi) Voormas it's the opposite of destructive and everyone want's to get his ass. Evil isn't destructive per se, evil it's BAD per se and destructive second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-22-2017, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T10:46:41-07:00","id":1142969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142895#post1142895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are mage factions, like the Aghori, that believe this and aren't Nephandi. BTW, the Aghori are evil, they do evil knowing that it's evil (it's not a case of bule/orange morality, they do evil BECAUSE it's Evil. They won't do it if they didn't believed it was evil) to trascend the ilusion of this world. That makes them evil.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those cases where Mage really stepped on its dick as far as cultural appropriation to a high degree of crapitude. The Aghori are an actual, real sect in India. They are not evil. They do not do evil for the sake of doing evil. They have a belief system that is rational both within its own confines and, with some explanation, to many other cultural mindsets. They do what many consider to be bizarre and anti-social things to face them and overcome then, thereby, by breaking taboo, to actually purify themselves and bring them closer to the godhead that is Shiva but is also immanent in every individual (because we are all Shiva). So, if shame is chain holding you back, go naked except for crematory ashes and never bathe. Oh and that one also destroys fear because it faces the ultimate fear, that of death, and minimizes to being a merely shameful thing. And so on... <br /> <br /> It's more than a little painful to see them depicted as the &quot;bad Euthanatos&quot; and see them come up when people start talking about the behavior ascribed to Nephandi. Aghori may do things that make people uncomfortable and may even seem disgusting, but they are not delighting in the suffering of the innocent in a Giles de Rais fashion. The Aghori sect of Euthanatos has less to do with the Aghori than it has to do with, say, the also not accurate thugees of Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom (with some actual Aghori sect practices as window dressing). <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T11:56:22-07:00","id":1142997,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't know the real life Aghori, but it wouldn't be the first time WoD does that kind of shit.<br /> <br /> Evil sects in WoD do tend to have an &quot;Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom&quot; vive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T12:14:26-07:00","id":1143001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142969#post1142969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is one of those cases where Mage really stepped on its dick as far as cultural appropriation to a high degree of crapitude. The Aghori are an actual, real sect in India. They are not evil. They do not do evil for the sake of doing evil. They have a belief system that is rational both within its own confines and, with some explanation, to many other cultural mindsets. They do what many consider to be bizarre and anti-social things to face them and overcome then, thereby, by breaking taboo, to actually purify themselves and bring them closer to the godhead that is Shiva but is also immanent in every individual (because we are all Shiva). So, if shame is chain holding you back, go naked except for crematory ashes and never bathe. Oh and that one also destroys fear because it faces the ultimate fear, that of death, and minimizes to being a merely shameful thing. And so on...<br /> <br /> It's more than a little painful to see them depicted as the &quot;bad Euthanatos&quot; and see them come up when people start talking about the behavior ascribed to Nephandi. Aghori may do things that make people uncomfortable and may even seem disgusting, but they are not delighting in the suffering of the innocent in a Giles de Rais fashion. The Aghori sect of Euthanatos has less to do with the Aghori than it has to do with, say, the also not accurate thugees of Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom (with some actual Aghori sect practices as window dressing).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is also true. Mage: The Ascension has an unfortunate habit of pigeon-holing certain groups into the &quot;Evil Group&quot; stereotype. And, in order to magnify the evil of the group, they make their methods more extreme or despicable, regardless of whether the actual, real-life groups did it. Often arbitrarily. Which is weird, given that many of the groups that are portrayed sympathetically in MtAs have methods that are just as unsavory or unsettling to most people as the ones that get the shaft. How are the Aghori (the real world ones, not the cartoonish charicatures) particularly more evil than the rest of the Euthanatos, who a large portion thereof habitually look for people to murder or mercy kill <i>as a matter of course</i>? <br /> <br /> It's the same sort of jump-the-gun decisions that labeled followers of Santa Muerte as being a Nephandic cult in M20, despite it being a movement that is pursued by millions (not just criminals, but normal people), both in Latin America and elsewhere. It's actually one of the religious movements that are actively growing in the modern age; and because veneration of Santa Muerte also involves elements of witchcraft (people pray to the Pale Lady for wealth, love, protection, revenge, etc.), you'd think that Mage would consider it a Big Deal for Traditionalists. When I wrote Magestuck, I just straight up made the decision to have the Euthanatos be working to fold Santa Muerte followers into their own Tradition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T16:29:28-07:00","id":1143078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1143001#post1143001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also true. Mage: The Ascension has an unfortunate habit of pigeon-holing certain groups into the &quot;Evil Group&quot; stereotype. And, in order to magnify the evil of the group, they make their methods more extreme or despicable, regardless of whether the actual, real-life groups did it. Often arbitrarily. Which is weird, given that many of the groups that are portrayed sympathetically in MtAs have methods that are just as unsavory or unsettling to most people as the ones that get the shaft. How are the Aghori (the real world ones, not the cartoonish charicatures) particularly more evil than the rest of the Euthanatos, who a large portion thereof habitually look for people to murder or mercy kill <i>as a matter of course</i>?<br /> <br /> It's the same sort of jump-the-gun decisions that labeled followers of Santa Muerte as being a Nephandic cult in M20, despite it being a movement that is pursued by millions (not just criminals, but normal people), both in Latin America and elsewhere. It's actually one of the religious movements that are actively growing in the modern age; and because veneration of Santa Muerte also involves elements of witchcraft (people pray to the Pale Lady for wealth, love, protection, revenge, etc.), you'd think that Mage would consider it a Big Deal for Traditionalists. When I wrote Magestuck, I just straight up made the decision to have the Euthanatos be working to fold Santa Muerte followers into their own Tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the Bata'a... If they include voudoun, hoodoo, candomble, santeria/brujeria, etc. there are significant commonalities with the followers of Santa Muerte and Jesus Malverde. And, while there is some crossover with criminal elements in their worshipers, that might not be a deal breaker for the other elements of culture and mystic praxis in the Bata'a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T17:46:16-07:00","id":1143098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142895#post1142895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, &quot;them being destructive&quot; it's an horrendous reason to kill Nephandi. Flambeau are destructive and you don't see them being persecuted. Aghori aren't very destructive (they torture to teach Ascencion), but evil, and the Extatics wage an internal war against them (and have presented a motion to declare them barabbi, a term normaly reserved for Nephandi) Voormas it's the opposite of destructive and everyone want's to get his ass. Evil isn't destructive per se, evil it's BAD per se and destructive second.</div> </div> </div> </div> Earlier in the same comment you say:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142895#post1142895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing about Nephandi that can be called &quot;destructive&quot; it's their end goal, but that's not what they <i>do</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Their end goal is destruction of the whole world. That makes them very different from Hermetics who like fire, and is a major reason most factions agree that they need to be stopped.<br /> <br /> As to two of my suggestions for possible Nephandi motivations being wrong--and in response to Bluecho's preference for Nephandi being just evil--I have an analogy. Major actions in Mage are like political parties. Political parties, to be viably large, need to take a &quot;big tent&quot; approach that includes a lot of people with different priorities. Someone might be a Democrat because they like sexual freedom, or because they favor more robust health intervention, or because they live in a big city and their peers vote Democrat. Likewise, a Mage might be a Technocrat because they think the arc of human progress is generally a good thing, or because they think rules and order are important, or because they worry about the safety of Sleepers--or because they're a would-be authoritarian.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi's stated philosophy of destroying the world because it is too static would probably appeal to some people who end up being Nephandi for that reason. But people who want to destroy the world for other reasons and quickly find out that just about every non-Nephandus has strong opinions against that--they're all just going to stick it out on their own? Maybe some of them. But the Nephandi are a relatively established group that could give some measure of protection. Likewise with the Alex DeLarges and Jubal Earlys of the world. A lot of mages who have little ideology beyond wanting to hurt people are going to be drawn into the Nephandi's big tent. All these groups don't have exactly the same goals, but they are all working toward roughly the same ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T18:06:00-07:00","id":1143101,"title":"","content":"I'll buy the Traditions, the Union, the Disparate Alliance and even the non-joiners (making no choice, is, after all, making a choice) as some analogues to the various choices one can make with politics, including the big tent analogy. But the Nephandi and Marauders are something altogether different. They aren't a collection of like-minded individuals along a continuum of &quot;like-minded&quot; where the ends may have little to nothing in common, who have come together for some greater purpose(s).<br /> <br /> But the Nephandi and Marauders aren't that. Both groups have to go through a second birth of sorts to become something different. For Marauders, it's something it's more of catastrophic epiphany that paradigm shifts them right off the board. For the Nephandi, it's literally a second birth with a reverse birth/rebirth overtly yanic sense. That's not what usually has to happen to one when one joins up with a political party. Or even a secret society. It's as decisive as an Awakening. It separates both groups from &quot;normal' mages as much as mages are from Sleepers. <br /> <br /> That's why it's a damn shame there's no actual crunch reflection of the Avatar Inversion for the Nephandi like there is for Marauders with Quiet. Without it, it does leave the Nephandi seeming as if they are just another group of mages united by something ideological up to and including &quot;These dudes may want to do some crazy shit, but, if I hang with them, they'll me do MY thing, so I'll join up.&quot; But they just aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T19:14:00-07:00","id":1143113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1143078#post1143078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or the Bata'a... If they include voudoun, hoodoo, candomble, santeria/brujeria, etc. there are significant commonalities with the followers of Santa Muerte and Jesus Malverde. And, while there is some crossover with criminal elements in their worshipers, that might not be a deal breaker for the other elements of culture and mystic praxis in the Bata'a.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, though personally I wouldn't agree that Santa Muerte veneration (or, indeed, Brujeria for that matter) quite fit with the religions and practices the Bata'a are into. I classify the latter as needing to have imported African beliefs somewhere in the syncretism in order to qualify. Whereas Brujeria - and Santa Muerte worship as a subset of same - is typified by specifically American native beliefs mixing with Catholicism. Without the African element, it's a sufficiently different beast that it should be approached as its own magical tradition. The elements of having been ripped from one's country of origin and enslaved in another are significant enough that it changes the ethos, and a faith that lacks that must be examined distinctly.<br /> <br /> Hence, why I tend to see practitioners of Brujeria and other native Latin American magics as falling more readily under other groups. The Celestial Chorus for those who take the rebranding of old gods into saints seriously (those for whom the Catholic part of their syncretism is important). The Verbana for those who worship the old gods AS the old gods. The Dreamspeakers for those who lean more towards animism and spirit work. And the Euthanatoi for those who specifically call upon Santa Muerte, as they literally venerate death.<br /> <br /> That said, all of this is our attempt to force a specific and living set of cultural practices into fictional organizations. In the context of Mage, it comes down to politics and a mage's self-identity. So I wouldn't say it's an invalid choice for a follower of Santa Muerte to join the Bata'a, or any other group, or even to try forming the own Craft, separate from all others.<br /> <br /> (I will also fully admit that my classification laid out in the first paragraph is an arbitrary one. I was just explaining why THIS arbitrary division between Santa Muerte and Greater Brujeria, and the African-derived faiths, is perhaps important from a thematic and cultural standpoint. You may, contrarily, maintain that the faiths being syncretic AT ALL are reason enough for Bruja and Brujo to team up with Bokors and Voodoonistas.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T07:19:11-07:00","id":1143221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142804#post1142804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand the frustration with the Nephandi being portrayed as exemplars of absolute evil. After all, the Technocracy went from being exemplars of absolute oppression to something more nuanced as the editions advanced and more supplemental material came out. It is a world defined by subjectivity. That's why I think &quot;evil&quot; is--while largely accurate--not the best way to describe the Nephandi. &quot;Destructive&quot; is a more useful concept that goes past subjective judgment. It also leaves room for more complexity, because they need to have reasons for why they want to destroy.<br /> <br /> Some possible Nephandic arguments for destroying everything (not all are mutually compatible):<br /> <br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the Nephandi can be treated and presented as a faction of dark True Mages, who do delve into - but not at all to the point of exclusivity - matters like sadism and suffering, and sometimes use them as Foci. What sets them apart as a group/faction is also their stance on mundane humans; and their attitude towards possible interactions with beings like demons, for example.<br /> The inclination to 'destroy the world' is not needed to make them deep; nor does it make them more interesting.<br /> <br /> As it is written now in much of Mage: The Ascension material, the Nephandi have lots of sentences all stating more or less &quot;They are bad.&quot; piled on in descriptions of them. The only sense I can make of much of this writings is that the writers want the Nephandi to be a group of True Mages that the players' characters can always kill on sight without second thoughts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1142643#post1142643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Senex does this each time someone says Amanda it's still a Nephandi and should be Gilguled. But why would he do a &quot;fake&quot; cure?, He's an Archmaster and the leader of a whole Tradition, he has all the power and prestige in the universe, what's the motivation?, what can he gain that he hasn't already?. If there's nothing to &quot;cure&quot; then obviously anyone on the power level to even matter to Senex would know about the ruse because no one would be able to prevent them from knowing. When you know how MASSIVELY powerful it's Senex the only reason to fake this would be to please his own stubbornness, to not admit that Nephandi can't be cured (as it goes against Good Death premises).</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot to mention that Senex believes, to an extent, in his own lies and propaganda about the Nephandi and the supposed help he can give to a Widderslainte. I guess this sets him apart from most snake oil salesmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-23-2017, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T09:04:18-07:00","id":1143245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1143221#post1143221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot to mention that Senex believes, to an extent, in his own lies and propaganda about the Nephandi and the supposed help he can give to a Widderslainte. I guess this sets him apart from most snake oil salesmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where, in any of the Amanda stories, do you get the idea that Senex does not believe in what he is doing? Your point is, essentially, that Amanda is an unreliable narrator. Actually, you are saying the author(s) is.are unreliable narrators. That what you are personally reading into the story is the superior and determinative reading despite the fact that there is very little to zero evidence that you are correct. Just standing on a mountain and shouting that Senex is a snake-oil salesman doesn't make it remotely true in anything other than your opinion.<br /> <br /> Which is now based on an argument that you have fundamentally undermined by adding the last caveat. Magic is ABOUT belief. If Senex believes his own lies and propaganda he's NOT a snake-oil salesman. A snake-oil salesman knows his snake oil doesn't work. That's the con. He's not conning anyone, unless, maybe it's himself. Which is undermined by the fact there is, in fact, additional evidence that Amanda, may, in fact, not be a Widderslainte anymore. And, oh, that's the POINT of the stories apparently. That nothing is certain in mage, even some of the &quot;rules&quot; like there is no coming back from the Cauls, and that there is no certainty that there is way to come back. (I mean, even if Senex was able to do so for Amanda, maybe it won't stick through to the next incarnation.... Or whatever).<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, you don't believe there is anything such as Widderslainte or Nephandi, in which case you are back to supporting the points that keep getting knocked down about the game designers being mustache-twirling villains behind the curtains rubbing their hands together laughing at all the gamers who have bought into their clever, clever attempt to deceive them about the things they say in the game books, except of course by the enlightened few who see through their devious (pointless?) plan.<br /> <br /> If you were to say something like, &quot;What if Senex is playing Mercedes/Amanda the whole time as a 'proof of concept' for the Widderslainte cure he's been working on?&quot; And he used his Archmastery of Entropy to find a mage he could push into becoming a Nephandi so he could try it out. With, using his mastery of the relevant Spheres, some idea of the probably outcome of his endeavors. Then he'd be a snake-oil salesman. But it wouldn't make the Nephandi not the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T09:33:23-07:00","id":1143249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1143113#post1143113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, though personally I wouldn't agree that Santa Muerte veneration (or, indeed, Brujeria for that matter) quite fit with the religions and practices the Bata'a are into. I classify the latter as needing to have imported African beliefs somewhere in the syncretism in order to qualify. Whereas Brujeria - and Santa Muerte worship as a subset of same - is typified by specifically American native beliefs mixing with Catholicism. Without the African element, it's a sufficiently different beast that it should be approached as its own magical tradition. The elements of having been ripped from one's country of origin and enslaved in another are significant enough that it changes the ethos, and a faith that lacks that must be examined distinctly.<br /> <br /> Hence, why I tend to see practitioners of Brujeria and other native Latin American magics as falling more readily under other groups. The Celestial Chorus for those who take the rebranding of old gods into saints seriously (those for whom the Catholic part of their syncretism is important). The Verbana for those who worship the old gods AS the old gods. The Dreamspeakers for those who lean more towards animism and spirit work. And the Euthanatoi for those who specifically call upon Santa Muerte, as they literally venerate death.<br /> <br /> That said, all of this is our attempt to force a specific and living set of cultural practices into fictional organizations. In the context of Mage, it comes down to politics and a mage's self-identity. So I wouldn't say it's an invalid choice for a follower of Santa Muerte to join the Bata'a, or any other group, or even to try forming the own Craft, separate from all others.<br /> <br /> (I will also fully admit that my classification laid out in the first paragraph is an arbitrary one. I was just explaining why THIS arbitrary division between Santa Muerte and Greater Brujeria, and the African-derived faiths, is perhaps important from a thematic and cultural standpoint. You may, contrarily, maintain that the faiths being syncretic AT ALL are reason enough for Bruja and Brujo to team up with Bokors and Voodoonistas.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little off-topic, but, I can see the Bata'a being open to embracing the followers of Santa Muerte because of the similarity in the fundamentals of being a mystic/religious tradition based on syncretism of European beliefs with those of an oppressed group in the context of colonialism and it's aftermath in the Americas. Though voudoun and hoodoo are almost entirely syncretic between African beliefs of the slaves and the European beliefs of their masters (specifically Catholic, but that weakens with hoodoo), there are other members of the Bata'a who come from syncretic faiths that included considerable influence from the beliefs of the indigenous peoples as well. There is an accident of history going on here.... There just weren't any more Native Caribbeans left when the slave trade that brought the Africans to the New World But in South America, there most certainly were, oftentimes the two groups were enslaved alongside or together. (And, with some aspects of hoodoo that there were some instances where Native North Americans and escaped slaves did combine beliefs to a degree, like in the Great Dismal Swamp)<br /> <br /> So, potentially, the Bata'a would see Santa Muerte as being very much like, say, some of the similar mystic traditions from South America. It's very much an Aztec/Catholic hybrid with a specific focus. So a hand might be extended in siblinghood. <br /> <br /> Sure, there may be an issue of various mages of Santa Muerte being pulled into various different groups, the Bata'a, the Dreamspeakers (since the Aztecs would have been sorted into the Dreamspeakers by the Traditions initially in the typical othering of non-Europeans back in the beginning), the Verbena (since there is DEFINITELY a lot going on that would make the magic between the two similar enough to argue for it), the Euthanatos (because, ya know, &quot;death mages&quot;) and, yes, the Nephandi and/or going it on their own as a potential new Craft. There is also the conceptual problem of how many mages there are, how many mages Awaken within or adopt the praxis of Santa Muerte beliefs and how that plays into the idea of Santa Muere mages being able to recognize each other and organize enough that there is the possibility of their identification as a discrete group. If the Santa Muerta mages don't internally organize, they are going to get drawn up into whatever group nabs them early on and integrated into that Sect. If they do organize (which seems to be the more basic assumption in Mage, e.g. that different mystic praxes self-identify and organize and the find some articulation with the existing Factions), they there would end up being some kind of selection process whereby a Sect and the Santa Muerte mages as a group would choose each other and they would become one of the constituent groups (like the House Bjornaer choosing the Verbena over the Order, House Luxor choosing to join up with the Etherites, etc.) or divide up (like the Valdaerman choosing to dissolve into Dreamspeakers, Verbena and Euthanatos).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T09:47:22-07:00","id":1143256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1141050#post1141050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At it's simplest, I see the Nephandi as True Mages who \u2013 unlike the Traditions or the Technocracy \u2013 have absolutely no illusions that you have to Awaken every single Sleeper as some kind of lofty goal. And some of the Sleepers / mundane humans have to be killed, of course. Maybe lots of them. And the Traditions - and others - call this outlook 'Descension'.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi are also unafraid to make pacts with entities that can be regarded as dark and/or alien, and to delve into areas of Magick such as demonology. This makes them hated by the Traditions and the Technocrats \u2013 and by the Order of Reason - and by most other True Mages. This is largely due to lack of understanding, superstitions, and jealousy.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, being a Nephandus is nothing like this.<br /> <br /> Nephandi are those mages that forsake their potential to Ascend, forever and ever, because of whatever reason brought them into the Caul. Barabbi don't usually know what truly a Nephandi or a Caul is when they find their Avatar inverted, and that's because Nephandi are sneaky sons of a bitch used to lie as easily as to breath and they can sell their medicine as the cure you're looking for. And once you're in there's no out, there's not even looking for an out because your whole soul is now pushing you toward the Nephandi's goal.<br /> <br /> The important thing to remember here is that the Ascension War is not what defines the Nephandi. If a Mage strives to overcome his mortal -or immortal- limits and become something greater than a god, Nephandi instead chose to bow under some other entity and be their servants forever. Powerful, dangerous servants, but servants nonetheless and nothing in the world or in any of their future incarnation is going to erase the mark of servitude from them. They had the chance to become more than just powerful and free themselves from the chains of the Tellurian, but gave up that chance when they became the Nephandi.<br /> If you're comfortable with the Exalted setting you should see an easy simile with the Abyssals.<br /> <br /> So, it's not really a &quot;who's the evilest&quot; contest that defines who's who, several mages can cause more evil or aim to bring even worse disasters on the world than the Nephandi (like Voormas in the Ascension plot, when he tried to destroy Telos). The difference is all a matter of potential and choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T10:31:31-07:00","id":1143272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1143256#post1143256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, no, being a Nephandus is nothing like this.<br /> <br /> Nephandi are those mages that forsake their potential to Ascend, forever and ever, because of whatever reason brought them into the Caul. Barabbi don't usually know what truly a Nephandi or a Caul is when they find their Avatar inverted, and that's because Nephandi are sneaky sons of a bitch used to lie as easily as to breath and they can sell their medicine as the cure you're looking for. And once you're in there's no out, there's not even looking for an out because your whole soul is now pushing you toward the Nephandi's goal.<br /> <br /> The important thing to remember here is that the Ascension War is not what defines the Nephandi. If a Mage strives to overcome his mortal -or immortal- limits and become something greater than a god, Nephandi instead chose to bow under some other entity and be their servants forever. Powerful, dangerous servants, but servants nonetheless and nothing in the world or in any of their future incarnation is going to erase the mark of servitude from them. They had the chance to become more than just powerful and free themselves from the chains of the Tellurian, but gave up that chance when they became the Nephandi.<br /> If you're comfortable with the Exalted setting you should see an easy simile with the Abyssals.<br /> <br /> So, it's not really a &quot;who's the evilest&quot; contest that defines who's who, several mages can cause more evil or aim to bring even worse disasters on the world than the Nephandi (like Voormas in the Ascension plot, when he tried to destroy Telos). The difference is all a matter of potential and choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there anything that makes these Nephandi that you described any different from Infernalists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T11:41:49-07:00","id":1143286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1143272#post1143272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything that makes these Nephandi that you described any different from Infernalists?</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur with this. I don't see the Nephandi as having to be subordinated to some lower power. Or even that that is the typical Nephandus. Or even, if the Nephandus in question is into that, that that is the source of their power.... Just because one chooses to willingly serve, that doesn't forfeit that which makes them a mage. Inverting an Avatar, whatever that might mean on a large scale, doesn't mean the Avatar merges with Cthulhu. It's just an Avatar with a different source code.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T16:25:59-07:00","id":1143350,"title":"","content":"I, too, disagree with the notion that Nephandi are naturally inclined towards subservience. They are still mages, albeit broken ones. And mages are free to determine their own Paradigm, whether that be one of self-actualization and apotheosis, or willing service to a higher (or, in this case, lower) power.<br /> <br /> It depends on their outlook and worldview, and how they contextualize their emotional drives (which, in this case, are towards evil). Some Nephandi may, like regular mages (and mortals in general, for that matter), decide that atheism is the most rational view of the universe. Or, if they acknowledge that there are greater powers in the universe, that they aren't deserving of the Nephandus's attention or loyalty. They may decide to pursue Descent on their own.<br /> <br /> Other Nephandi may find fulfillment in serving powers greater than themselves. In a similar way that normal people find joy and comfort in a god or gods, a Nephandus may so find joy and comfort in the belief in dark gods or infernal powers. Especially if those lower powers or alien beings resonate with the same black, despicable values that the Fallen feel innately. It is gratifying for a Nephandus who loves to revel and kill to have a dark god from outside the universe who encourages reveling and killing, and would teach the Nephandus new ways to revel and kill if the mage would only help them enter the universe.<br /> <br /> Still other Nephandi - like the Infernalists - may not particularly like or dislike demons, but simply find it pragmatic to work with them. Seeing their patrons, less as things to be worshiped, but as business partners. They figure that if the demons turn the world into an extension of Actual Hell, that would be pretty grand (since it would mean humanity would suffer for all eternity). But of course, the Infernalist doesn't really want to be part of those suffering masses. So they figure, if they work with the demons now and help them bring out hell on earth, they could score themselves more comfortable positions in the new world order. Until that day comes, they can get plenty of fringe benefits from working with hell. Plus, they may figure, &quot;Hell, I'm damned anyway, might as well get my damnation's worth now while I still can&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T22:12:38-07:00","id":1143399,"title":"","content":"I like Ander Wood's idea about the Nephandi and Deep Umbral entities--that more often than not, the Nephandi have the upper hand in the relationship. The fallen Mages have more access to Earth, more understanding of humans, and more understanding of how reality works here. Also in a game that makes a big deal of human potential, the potential of an Awakened human for evil is probably higher even than that of a dark god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T03:29:58-07:00","id":1143428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128752-nephandi?p=1143272#post1143272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything that makes these Nephandi that you described any different from Infernalists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the Nephandi are, actually, Infernal Nephandi. The others just serve different masters. There are, though, two main differences with non-nephandi Infernalists.<br /> <br /> First, the Avatar: Infernalists have their same regular Avatar, struggling for Ascension, on which the demons have some right; demons may have enough rights to actually command it, but it's not like the Avatar (and therefore the Mage's soul and true drive) is willing to obey, he just have to. So you have a Mage willing to serve demons with an unwilling Avatar. Nephandi, having an inverted Avatar, are instead naturally driven toward their masters' desires (like in the widderslainte case, with the Avatar poisoning the mage's personality from the very start).<br /> <br /> Second, the will: Infernalists have bound themselves in servitude for power (on their current incarnation), while Nephandi have a more complex approach to their masters. Quoting from the M20:<br /> &quot;They don\u2019t serve Outer Gods, in truth. Nephandi simply recognize such beings as reflections of their own Enlightenment\u2026 a savage wisdom that sees the Absolute in every living thing and knows what\u2019s waiting at the end of All.&quot;<br /> So, it's more like recognizing that your true nature is embodied by a specific alien entity in the Deep Umbra. You're still serving it, but your unity of intent makes you act more as allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}